"""
Brevo email setup

This project supports Brevo in two ways:

1. Brevo SMTP relay
2. Brevo through Anymail

Use only one setup at a time.

Brevo SMTP setup

Use this if you want Brevo to work like a standard SMTP provider.

1. Sign in to Brevo.
2. Open Settings.
3. Go to SMTP and API.
4. Generate an SMTP key.
5. Set these environment values:

EMAIL_BACKEND=django.core.mail.backends.smtp.EmailBackend
EMAIL_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
EMAIL_PORT=587
EMAIL_USE_TLS=True
EMAIL_HOST_USER=apikey
EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD=your-brevo-smtp-key
DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL=verified-sender@example.com

Brevo Anymail setup

Use this if you want Django to send email through the Brevo API.

1. Make sure Anymail is installed.
2. Add anymail to INSTALLED_APPS.
3. Set the Brevo API key in your environment.
4. Switch Django to the Anymail backend.

Example environment values:

EMAIL_BACKEND=anymail.backends.brevo.EmailBackend
BREVO_API_KEY=your-brevo-api-key
DEFAULT_FROM_EMAIL=verified-sender@example.com

How to switch

If you want SMTP, use the SMTP block and remove or override the Anymail values.
If you want Anymail, use the Anymail block and keep BREVO_API_KEY in the environment.

Project note

The production settings already read BREVO_API_KEY and default to the Brevo Anymail backend.
###To view sent,failed,delivered emails
1. Sign in to Brevo.
2. On the dashboard click transactional >Realtime

